  "body": "## Finding description and impact \n\n`MevCapture` extension records tick in the pool at the beginning of the block and after every swap takes additional fee proportional to the distance between tick after the swap and tick at the beginning of the block.\nUsers can swap  using exactOut swaps or exactIn swaps.\nIn mev capture when user is swapping using exactIn swap, the additional Mev capture fee is taken on the output amount.\nWhen user is swapping using exactOutput swap, the additional Mev capture fee is added to the input amount.\n\nThis leads to situation where most of the time one of the paths (ExactIn swap, ExactOut swap) overpays/underpays in comparison to the other.\n\nAs lets imagine that at the beginning of the block, pool is at tick X.\n\n**ExactIn scenario** :  User wants to swap using exactIn providing `amountIn` amount of tokens. In the pool the actual priceImpactAmount is `amountIn` - fee. Price Impact amount moves the price by some Z amount of ticks. The `amount out` is calculated and returned to the Mev capture. Mev capture based on the distance between tick in the pool and tick at the beginning of the block ( |X + Z - X | * fee) takes additional fee from `amount out`. So `amountOut` = `amountOut` - additionalFee\n\n**ExactOut scenario**:\nNow what if instead of exactIn swap, user would perform an exactOut swap with exact output amount = `amountOut` - additionalFee ? :\nMev capture will first swap using Core. Then inside the core :\nBecause the `amountOut-additionalFee` is smaller than the amountOut from the previous scenario, the amountIn required to get this exact out amount of tokens is also smaller.  This means that actual price impact will be smaller, this leads to situation where price is moved by G ticks and G < Z.\nAfter the swap in the core, Mev capture based on the distance between tick in the pool and the tick at the beginning at the block (|X+ G - X| * fee) adds additional fee to `amountIn`. So `amountIn` += additionalFee\n\nSo exact output swap in this scenario will move price by less ticks, so while receiving the same amount of output tokens it will pay less amount of token in.\n\nI added POC that illustrates the scenario outlined above showing that in this scenario exact Out is superior.\n\nThis finding shows that certain users will overpay/underpay compared to others, leading to the loss/gain for some of them and unexpected results.\n\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nChange the fee mechanism, so that exactIn/exactOut swaps have the same outcome or maybe allow only one of the exactIn/exactOut swaps.",
  "proof_of_concept": "This POC should be put inside test/extensions folder. One can observe console.logs and see that two test_in and test_out cases require different amount input tokens while giving the same amount of output tokens due to reasons outlined above.\n\n```solidity\n\n\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: ekubo-license-v1.eth\npragma solidity >=0.8.30;\n\nimport {createSwapParameters} from \"../../src/types/swapParameters.sol\";\nimport {UsesCore} from \"../../src/base/UsesCore.sol\";\nimport {PoolKey} from \"../../src/types/poolKey.sol\";\nimport {PoolConfig, createConcentratedPoolConfig, createStableswapPoolConfig} from \"../../src/types/poolConfig.sol\";\nimport {PoolId} from \"../../src/types/poolId.sol\";\nimport {SqrtRatio} from \"../../src/types/sqrtRatio.sol\";\nimport {MIN_TICK, MAX_TICK, MAX_TICK_SPACING} from \"../../src/math/constants.sol\";\nimport {FullTest} from \"../FullTest.sol\";\nimport {MEVCapture, mevCaptureCallPoints} from \"../../src/extensions/MEVCapture.sol\";\nimport {IMEVCapture} from \"../../src/interfaces/extensions/IMEVCapture.sol\";\nimport {CoreLib} from \"../../src/libraries/CoreLib.sol\";\nimport {ExposedStorageLib} from \"../../src/libraries/ExposedStorageLib.sol\";\nimport {MEVCaptureRouter} from \"../../src/MEVCaptureRouter.sol\";\nimport {MEVCapturePoolState} from \"../../src/types/mevCapturePoolState.sol\";\nimport {PoolBalanceUpdate} from \"../../src/types/poolBalanceUpdate.sol\";\nimport {console} from \"forge-std/console.sol\";\n\nabstract contract BaseMEVCaptureTest is FullTest {\n    MEVCapture internal mevCapture;\n\n    function setUp() public virtual override {\n        FullTest.setUp();\n        address deployAddress = address(uint160(mevCaptureCallPoints().toUint8()) << 152);\n        deployCodeTo(\"MEVCapture.sol\", abi.encode(core), deployAddress);\n        mevCapture = MEVCapture(deployAddress);\n        router = new MEVCaptureRouter(core, address(mevCapture));\n    }\n\n    function coolAllContracts() internal virtual override {\n        FullTest.coolAllContracts();\n        vm.cool(address(mevCapture));\n    }\n\n    function createMEVCapturePool(uint64 fee, uint32 tickSpacing, int32 tick)\n        internal\n        returns (PoolKey memory poolKey)\n    {\n        poolKey = createPool(\n            address(token0), address(token1), tick, createConcentratedPoolConfig(fee, tickSpacing, address(mevCapture))\n        );\n    }\n}\n\ncontract MyMEV is BaseMEVCaptureTest {\n    using CoreLib for *;\n    using ExposedStorageLib for *;\n\n    function test_isRegistered() public view {\n        assertTrue(core.isExtensionRegistered(address(mevCapture)));\n    }\n\n    function getPoolState(PoolId poolId) private view returns (MEVCapturePoolState state) {\n        state = MEVCapturePoolState.wrap(mevCapture.sload(PoolId.unwrap(poolId)));\n    }\n    function test_in() public {\n         int32 startingTick = 0;\n        PoolKey memory poolKey =\n            createMEVCapturePool({fee: uint64(uint256(1 << 64) / 100), tickSpacing: 20_000, tick: startingTick});\n        createPosition(poolKey, -100_000, 100_000, 1_000_000, 1_000_000);\n\n        token0.approve(address(router), type(uint256).max);\n        coolAllContracts();\n        PoolBalanceUpdate balanceUpdate = router.swap({\n            poolKey: poolKey,\n            params: createSwapParameters({\n                _isToken1: false, _amount: 500_000, _sqrtRatioLimit: SqrtRatio.wrap(0), _skipAhead: 0\n            }),\n            calculatedAmountThreshold: type(int256).min,\n            recipient: address(this)\n        });\n        vm.snapshotGasLastCall(\"input_token0_move_tick_spacings\");\n        console.log(\"delta 0:\", balanceUpdate.delta0());\n        console.log(\"delta 1:\",balanceUpdate.delta1());\n        assertEq(balanceUpdate.delta0(), 500_000);\n        assertEq(balanceUpdate.delta1(), -471_801);\n        int32 tick = core.poolState(poolKey.toPoolId()).tick();\n         console.log(\"starting tick:\", startingTick);\n        console.log(\"tick:\", tick);\n    }\n\n    function test_out() public {\n        int32 startingTick = 0;\n        PoolKey memory poolKey =\n            createMEVCapturePool({fee: uint64(uint256(1 << 64) / 100), tickSpacing: 20_000, tick: startingTick});\n        createPosition(poolKey, -100_000, 100_000, 1_000_000, 1_000_000);\n\n        token0.approve(address(router), type(uint256).max);\n        coolAllContracts();\n        PoolBalanceUpdate balanceUpdate = router.swap({\n            poolKey: poolKey,\n            params: createSwapParameters({\n                _isToken1: true, _amount: -471_801, _sqrtRatioLimit: SqrtRatio.wrap(0), _skipAhead: 0\n            }),\n            calculatedAmountThreshold: type(int256).min,\n            recipient: address(this)\n        });\n        console.log(\"delta 0:\", balanceUpdate.delta0());\n        console.log(\"delta 1:\",balanceUpdate.delta1());\n        int32 tick = core.poolState(poolKey.toPoolId()).tick();\n         console.log(\"starting tick:\", startingTick);\n       console.log(\"tick after swap:\", tick);\n    }\n}\n\n```",
